1081	{"artifactId":"PLAN-8315a11f29fd2812-s3","entry":{"id":"9d47a246","text":"Amended 2026-10-20 by the stakeholder's decision after t2's third build gate. t2's check required a correction note on every re-issue, which conflicts with s1's approved rule: prepare lets one symbol fill the hard limit, and a correction that does not fit beside such a call is left out and logged, never cut. The check now follows s1: the reasons have a fixed size (a made-up value is located by count and position, never quoted back), so the correction is sent whenever the call has room; a call that already fills the limit is re-issued as planned with the omission logged, and a second invalid answer still fails the review. Also recorded: commit 581e1d76 (a t2 fix) changed quality's description reasons to the same fixed-size form for consistency, since every chunk validator lives in one module; that part belongs to t3's surface.","actor":{"id":"legacy:subho-ghosh","kind":"person","properties":{"name":"Subho Ghosh"}},"timestamp":"2026-10-20T18:00:07.782Z","feedback":[],"kind":"revision-request"}}
593	{"artifactId":"PLAN-8315a11f29fd2812-s3","entry":{"id":"872179b1","text":"Amended 2026-10-21: t7 follows the approved LLD on note ids (stakeholder option A, 2026-10-20): merge never rewrites a location; a gather finding located at an evidence note id is re-asked, then fails the review. The note-id expansion wording in t7 (check, summary, test name, coverage row) was missed when the LLD was amended; it is corrected here.","actor":{"id":"legacy:subho-ghosh","kind":"person","properties":{"name":"Subho Ghosh"}},"timestamp":"2026-10-21T04:28:16.013Z","feedback":[],"kind":"revision-request"}}
